<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌞 LIVE SOLAR RADIATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE SOLAR RADIATION</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/solar_radiation/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Surface downward shortwave solar radiation (W/m^2), RAP hourly estimate, FIXED absolute scale 0&ndash;1000+: night <b>0</b> (near-black) &rarr; <b>150</b> &rarr; <b>300</b> &rarr; <b>450</b> &rarr; <b>600</b> &rarr; <b>750</b> &rarr; extreme <b>1000+</b> (near-white). <b>LOWEST 0</b>, <b>HIGHEST+ 1000+</b>. Same flux always shows the same color. Values shown exactly as observed; night reads zero; clouds reduce values quantitatively. Broadband sunlight: includes ultraviolet, visible, and near-infrared energy. This is not a UV Index and not a visible-light meter reading. Hourly weather-model estimate, not a ground sensor measurement at every location.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP RAP (Rapid Refresh) hourly surface DSWRF (downward short-wave radiation flux)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 01:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> rap-20260926-t17z-f01<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌞 LIVE SOLAR RADIATION — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Solar_Radiation.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
